      "description": "Job Placement for Grads Surpasses 90% for 10th Straight Year - University of the Ozarks Skip to main content Join us for Homecoming! October 15-18 Click here to check out the details! Ozarks Experience Ozarks Email Calendar Directory TSC Search Ozarks.edu: Narrow your search by content type Page Degrees Events News Offices & Services Faculty & Staff Links Menu University of the Ozarks Home Admissions & Aid Show sub-menu Learn about our admissions process, financial aid and begin your Ozarks journey. Admissions & Aid Costs & Aid How to Apply Visit Campus New Student Orientation & Move-In High School Juniors Incoming Freshman Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Calendar Apply Academics Show sub-menu Learn about our unique academic experience and the academic opportunities here at University of the Ozarks. Academics Our Academic Experience Degrees & Programs LENS Program Compass Study Abroad Library Canvas Student Success Center Jones Learning Center Faculty Directory Calendar Apply Life at Ozarks Show sub-menu Explore what makes life at Ozarks so special. Life at Ozarks Important Dates New Student Orientation & Move-In Student Engagement Residential Life & Housing Dining Shuttle Services Campus Recreation Spiritual Life Career Services Counseling Services Campus & Region Map Public Safety Title IX Calendar Apply Athletics Show sub-menu Our student-athletes strive for excellence on and off of the playing field, court or pool. Athletics Athletics Website Intercollegiate Sports Schedules Athlete Recruitment Eagle Tuesdays Fitness Facilities Support Athletics Recruit Me Support Show sub-menu Your gifts to University of the Ozarks truly matter to our students! Support Ways to Support Green Giving Update your info Grants and Initiatives Advancement Staff Hire an Eagle 1834 Society Planned Giving Give Bookstore Show sub-menu Our campus store located in Robson Library next to Campus Perks. Shop Now Conference Services Show sub-menu Ozarks offers a prime location for a variety of events. Contact us today to see how we can help make your next event a success. Conference Services Conferences and Meetings Weddings and Receptions Camps Catering Internal Events Contact Us! About Show sub-menu Learn about our thriving university, staff and history. About Leadership History Mission and Vision Our Christian Heritage Board of Trustees Rankings and Accreditations Student Outcomes Strategic Plan News Location & Directions Personnel Directory Offices & Services Marketing and Public Relations Reporting Calendar Request Info Search Ozarks.edu: Links Current Students Admitted Students Parents Faculty and Staff Alumni Search Request Info Visit Give Apply Home / News / Job Placement for Grads Surpasses 90% for 10th Straight Year Job Placement for Grads Surpasses 90% for 10th Straight Year July 28, 2026 By Larry Isch Posted in Career Services For the 10th consecutive year, the initial employment and graduate school placement success rate of recent University of the Ozarks graduates exceeds 90 percent, according to the University’s 2026 First Destination and Career Profile Report. The latest survey looks at the Class of 2025 U of O graduates and whether or not they had employment or were in graduate or professional school within six months of graduation. The report found that 92 percent of the respondents had either full-time employment, were in graduate or professional school or were employed part-time. Out of 173 graduates, 14 were still seeking employment at the time of the survey. According to the latest report (2025) from the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE), the national average is 86 percent for employment and graduate school placement. It is the 10th consecutive year that U of O’s success rate for its graduates has exceeded 90 percent. The average success rate for the University over the past five years is 94 percent. “For more than a decade, we have maintained a greater than 90 percent success rate on the First Destination Survey, meaning that over 90 percent of our graduates secure part-time or full-time employment, pursue advanced degree programs, or enter military service within six months of graduation,” said Matt Bewley, director of career services. “This consistent achievement reflects the strength of our academic programs, the dedication of our faculty and staff, and the intentional career preparation embedded throughout the student experience. It also demonstrates our ongoing commitment to equipping students with the skills, confidence, and connections they need to thrive after graduation.” According to the 2026 First Destination and Career Profile Report, the 2025 graduates were working in 20 states and 12 countries. In addition, 34 members of the Class of 2025 were in graduate or professional schools in nine different states and two other countries. The largest number of employed graduates were in the professional fields of K-12 education (24), healthcare (21), retail and customer service (17), marketing (8) and environmental services (8). The University follows the NACE standards and protocols for the collection and dissemination of initial career outcomes for recent graduates. Topics: Career Services Share this story News Categories News Categories Select News Category About  (866) Academic Support  (34) Academics  (292) Accounting  (9) Admission  (32) Alumni  (218) Alumni Stories  (41) American Studies  (4) Art  (168) Athletics  (2,827) Biology  (73) Business Administration  (92) Business Education  (1) Campaign  (17) Campus Life  (39) Career Services  (17) Chapel  (46) Chemistry  (26) Communication Studies  (84) Community Events  (404) Community Service  (66) Computer Science  (6) Cost & Aid  (3) COVID-19  (8) Creative Writing / Thought  (6) Criminal Justice  (4) Donor Spotlights  (8) Economics  (3) Education  (73) Elementary Education  (12) English  (22) Environmental Studies  (39) Exercise Science  (1) Exhibit  (70) Faculty Spo