brary next to Campus Perks. Shop Now Conference Services Show sub-menu Ozarks offers a prime location for a variety of events. Contact us today to see how we can help make your next event a success. Conference Services Conferences and Meetings Weddings and Receptions Camps Catering Internal Events Contact Us! About Show sub-menu Learn about our thriving university, staff and history. About Leadership History Mission and Vision Our Christian Heritage Board of Trustees Rankings and Accreditations Student Outcomes Strategic Plan News Location & Directions Personnel Directory Offices & Services Marketing and Public Relations Reporting Calendar Request Info Search Ozarks.edu: Links Current Students Admitted Students Parents Faculty and Staff Alumni Search Request Info Visit Give Apply Home / News / Bruce Joins Ozarks as Mental Health Therapist Bruce Joins Ozarks as Mental Health Therapist August 18, 2026 By Larry Isch Posted in Student Support Services Joy Bruce has joined University of the Ozarks as a mental health therapist. Her first day was Aug. 17. Dr. Kaethe Hoehling will continue to serve as the director of counseling services in a part-time role for the 2026-27 academic year. A native of Texarkana, Texas, Bruce earned a degree in psychology from University of Arkansas and a master’s degree in clinical mental health counseling from Walden University. She has most recently worked at Pinnacle Point Behavioral Healthcare and served as a graduate internship with Kornerstone Counseling in Russellville, Ark. She has also worked at the Cornerstone Counseling Clinic in Texarkana and the Piney Ridge Treatment Center in Fayetteville, Ark. “I remember what it was like to start over in college, move to a new town, and navigate a completely new chapter of life,” Bruce said. “I’m excited to join University of the Ozarks and have the opportunity to support students during such an important time in their lives by being a safe and supportive place for students who may be going through a difficult time.” She has a young son named Beckham and a fiance, Ryan. Outside of work, Bruce enjoys finding creative ways to relax and spend time with the people she loves. “Every Saturday I go to music class with my toddler and it’s the highlight of my week,” she said. Topics: Student Support Services Share this story News Categories News Categories Select News Category About  (866) Academic Support  (34) Academics  (292) Accounting  (9) Admission  (32) Alumni  (218) Alumni Stories  (42) American Studies  (4) Art  (168) Athletics  (2,827) Biology  (73) Business Administration  (92) Business Education  (1) Campaign  (17) Campus Life  (39) Career Services  (17) Chapel  (46) Chemistry  (26) Communication Studies  (84) Community Events  (404) Community Service  (66) Computer Science  (6) Cost & Aid  (3) COVID-19  (8) Creative Writing / Thought  (6) Criminal Justice  (4) Donor Spotlights  (8) Economics  (3) Education  (73) Elementary Education  (12) English  (22) Environmental Studies  (39) Exercise Science  (1) Exhibit  (70) Faculty Spotlights  (51) Film Studies  (4) Finance  (1) Financial Aid  (15) Giving  (99) Graphic Design  (1) Greystone  (3) Health Science  (35) History  (13) Information Science  (2) Interfaith Studies  (14) International  (16) Internships  (21) JLC  (54) Management  (9) Marketing  (15) Mathematics  (35) Media Production  (8) Military Science  (3) Music  (52) Music Performance  (15) Music Studies  (4) Outdoors  (25) Parents  (9) PE  (4) Philosophy  (15) Photography  (5) Physical Education  (4) Physics  (7) Political Science  (48) Presbyterian  (47) Psychology  (40) Religion  (17) Robson Library  (2) ROTC  (2) Scholarship  (32) Skills Academy  (1) Sociology  (14) Spanish  (16) Strategic Communication  (3) Student Events  (126) Student Life  (35) Student Organizations  (100) Student Stories  (66) Student Support Services  (4) Study Abroad  (21) Sustainable Agriculture  (6) Theatre  (133) Traditions  (42) Tuition  (4) Volunteer  (1) WAIS  (43