      "title": "Lilly Endowment Makes $500K Gift to Support Town Square Collaborative",
      "description": "Lilly Endowment Makes $500K Gift to Support Town Square Collaborative - University of the Ozarks Skip to main content Enable accessibility for low vision Open the accessibility menu Skip to main content Join us for Homecoming! October 15-18 Click here to check out the details! Ozarks Experience Ozarks Email Calendar Directory TSC Search Ozarks.edu: Narrow your search by content type Page Degrees Events News Offices & Services Faculty & Staff Links Menu University of the Ozarks Home Admissions & Aid Show sub-menu Learn about our admissions process, financial aid and begin your Ozarks journey. Admissions & Aid Costs & Aid How to Apply Visit Campus New Student Orientation & Move-In High School Juniors Incoming Freshman Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Calendar Apply Academics Show sub-menu Learn about our unique academic experience and the academic opportunities here at University of the Ozarks. Academics Our Academic Experience Degrees & Programs LENS Program Compass Study Abroad Library Canvas Student Success Center Jones Learning Center Faculty Directory Calendar Apply Life at Ozarks Show sub-menu Explore what makes life at Ozarks so special. Life at Ozarks Important Dates New Student Orientation & Move-In Student Engagement Residential Life & Housing Dining Shuttle Services Campus Recreation Spiritual Life Career Services Counseling Services Campus & Region Map Public Safety Title IX Calendar Apply Athletics Show sub-menu Our student-athletes strive for excellence on and off of the playing field, court or pool. Athletics Athletics Website Intercollegiate Sports Schedules Athlete Recruitment Eagle Tuesdays Fitness Facilities Support Athletics Recruit Me Support Show sub-menu Your gifts to University of the Ozarks truly matter to our students! Support Ways to Support Green Giving Update your info Grants and Initiatives Advancement Staff Hire an Eagle 1834 Society Planned Giving Give Bookstore Show sub-menu Our campus store located in Robson Library next to Campus Perks. Shop Now Conference Services Show sub-menu Ozarks offers a prime location for a variety of events. Contact us today to see how we can help make your next event a success. Conference Services Conferences and Meetings Weddings and Receptions Camps Catering Internal Events Contact Us! About Show sub-menu Learn about our thriving university, staff and history. About Leadership History Mission and Vision Our Christian Heritage Board of Trustees Rankings and Accreditations Student Outcomes Strategic Plan News Location & Directions Personnel Directory Offices & Services Marketing and Public Relations Reporting Calendar Request Info Search Ozarks.edu: Links Current Students Admitted Students Parents Faculty and Staff Alumni Search Request Info Visit Give Apply Home / News / Lilly Endowment Makes $500K Gift to Support Town Square Collaborative Lilly Endowment Makes $500K Gift to Support Town Square Collaborative August 13, 2026 By Larry Isch Posted in About University of the Ozarks has received a grant of $500,000 from Lilly Endowment Inc., to support the continuation of the Arkansas Presbytery Thriving in Ministry program, which is a part of the University’s Town Square Collaborative. Lilly Endowment made the grant through its Thriving in Ministry initiative, which supports a variety of religious organizations across the nation as they create or strengthen programs that help pastors build relationships with experienced clergy who can serve as mentors and guide them through key leadership challenges in congregational ministry. The Arkansas Presbytery Thriving in Ministry program at U of O was established in 2021 through an initial gift of nearly $1 million from Lilly Endowment to assist and support rural pastors within the Arkansas Presbytery in areas such as launching new churches and serving small membership churches. Going forward, the Thriving in Ministry program within the Town Square Collaborative will support pastors and church leaders throughout the Presbytery of Arkansas. “We are delighted to receive an additional support from Lilly Endowment to continue the work of this program,” said Rev. Phillip Blackburn, director of the Town Square Collaborative. “Our work with congregational leaders in the Presbytery of Arkansas will continue for another five years, and we will be able to apply the many lessons learned. Clergy and church leaders need support, and I am honored to be at an institution which recognizes their important contributions and seeks to support them going forward.” Ozarks has received more than $6 million from the Lilly Endowment since 2020 for a series of related programs and initiatives aimed at providing resources to help churches in rural areas and small towns, including the Ministry in Rural Areas and Small Towns Initiative in 2023 which helps rural churches embrace their calling as anchor institutions within their communities. Together, these gifts are housed within the Town Square Collaborative ( www.townsquareco.org ). Lilly Endowment is an Indianapolis-based private philanthropic foundation created in 1937 by J.K. Lilly Sr. and sons Eli and J.K. Jr. through gifts of stock in their pharmaceutical business, Eli Lilly & Company. While those gifts remain the financial bedrock of the Endowment, the Endowment is a separate entity from the company, with a distinct governing board, staff and location. In keeping with the founders’ wishes, the Endowment supports the causes of community development, education and religion. Although the Endowment maintains a special commitment to its hometown, Indianapolis, and home state, Indiana, it also funds programs throughout the United States, especially in the field of religion. While the primary aim of its religion grantmaking focuses on strengthening the leadership and vitality of Christian Congregations in the United States, the Endowment also seeks to foster public understanding of about religion and lift up in fair, accurate and balanced ways the contributions that people of all faiths and various religious communities play on the United States and around the globe. Topics: About Share this story News Categories News Categories Select News Category About  (866) Academic Support  (34) Academics  (292) Accounting  (9) Admission  (32) Alumni  (219) Alumni Stories  (42) American Studies  (4) Art  (168) Athletics  (2,827) Biology  (73) Business Administration  (92) Business Education  (1) Campaign  (17) Campus Life  (39) Career Services  (17) Chapel  (46) Chemistry  (26) Communication Studies  (84) Community Events  (404) Community Service  (66) Computer Science  (6) Cost & Aid  (3) COVID-19  (8) Creative Writing / Thought  (6) Criminal Justice  (4) Donor Spotlights  (8) Economics  (3) Education  (73) Elementary Education  (12) English  (22) Environmental Studies  (39) Exercise Science  (1) Exhibit  (70) Faculty Spotlights  (51) Film Studies  (4) Finance  (1) Financial Aid  (15) Giving  (99) Graphic Design  (1) Greystone  (3) Health Science  (35) History  (13) Information Science  (2) Interfaith Studies  (14) International  (16) Internships  (21) JLC  (54) Management  (9) Marketing  (15) Mathematics  (35) Media Production  (8) Military Science  (3) Music  (52) Music Performance  (15) Music Studies  (4) Outdoors  (25) Parents  (9) PE  (4) Philosophy  (15) Photography  (5) Physical Education  (4) Physics  (7) Political Science  (48) Presbyterian  (47) Psychology  (40) Religion  (17) Robson Library  (2) ROTC  (2) Scholarship  (32) Skills Academy  (1) Sociology  (14) Spanish  (16) Strategic Communication  (3) Student Events  (126) Student Life  (35) Student Organizations  (100) Student Stories  (66) Student Support Services  (4) Study Abroad  (21) Sustainable Agriculture  (6) Theatre  (133) Traditions  (42) Tuition  (4) Volunteer  (1) WAIS  (43) News Archives News Archives Select Month September 2026 August 2026 July 2026 June 2026 May 2026 April 2026 March 2026 February 2026 January 2026 D