      "title": "U of O Enhances Student Experience with MacBook Neo Initiative",
      "description": "U of O Enhances Student Experience with MacBook Neo Initiative - University of the Ozarks Skip to main content Enable accessibility for low vision Open the accessibility menu Skip to main content Join us for Homecoming! October 15-18 Click here to check out the details! Ozarks Experience Ozarks Email Calendar Directory TSC Search Ozarks.edu: Narrow your search by content type Page Degrees Events News Offices & Services Faculty & Staff Links Menu University of the Ozarks Home Admissions & Aid Show sub-menu Learn about our admissions process, financial aid and begin your Ozarks journey. Admissions & Aid Costs & Aid How to Apply Visit Campus New Student Orientation & Move-In High School Juniors Incoming Freshman Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Calendar Apply Academics Show sub-menu Learn about our unique academic experience and the academic opportunities here at University of the Ozarks. Academics Our Academic Experience Degrees & Programs LENS Program Compass Study Abroad Library Canvas Student Success Center Jones Learning Center Faculty Directory Calendar Apply Life at Ozarks Show sub-menu Explore what makes life at Ozarks so special. Life at Ozarks Important Dates New Student Orientation & Move-In Student Engagement Residential Life & Housing Dining Shuttle Services Campus Recreation Spiritual Life Career Services Counseling Services Campus & Region Map Public Safety Title IX Calendar Apply Athletics Show sub-menu Our student-athletes strive for excellence on and off of the playing field, court or pool. Athletics Athletics Website Intercollegiate Sports Schedules Athlete Recruitment Eagle Tuesdays Fitness Facilities Support Athletics Recruit Me Support Show sub-menu Your gifts to University of the Ozarks truly matter to our students! Support Ways to Support Green Giving Update your info Grants and Initiatives Advancement Staff Hire an Eagle 1834 Society Planned Giving Give Bookstore Show sub-menu Our campus store located in Robson Library next to Campus Perks. Shop Now Conference Services Show sub-menu Ozarks offers a prime location for a variety of events. Contact us today to see how we can help make your next event a success. Conference Services Conferences and Meetings Weddings and Receptions Camps Catering Internal Events Contact Us! About Show sub-menu Learn about our thriving university, staff and history. About Leadership History Mission and Vision Our Christian Heritage Board of Trustees Rankings and Accreditations Student Outcomes Strategic Plan News Location & Directions Personnel Directory Offices & Services Marketing and Public Relations Reporting Calendar Request Info Search Ozarks.edu: Links Current Students Admitted Students Parents Faculty and Staff Alumni Search Request Info Visit Give Apply Home / News / U of O Enhances Student Experience with MacBook Neo Initiative U of O Enhances Student Experience with MacBook Neo Initiative August 7, 2026 By Larry Isch Posted in Academic Support Beginning with the Fall 2026 Semester, University of the Ozarks will equip every incoming full-time, first-year student with a new Apple MacBook Neo, ensuring they arrive on campus with the technology needed to learn, create and succeed from the first day of classes. The initiative replaces the University’s previous program of providing new students with iPads and reflects Ozarks’ continued commitment to removing barriers to student success while enhancing the overall academic experience. By providing every new student with the same high-quality laptop, the University is ensuring that all students—regardless of financial circumstances or academic major—have immediate access to the software, computing power and digital resources required for college-level work. University officials said the initiative builds on Ozarks’ long-standing commitment to access, inclusion and student success by eliminating a significant upfront expense for families while creating a more equitable learning environment. “We’ve transitioned from providing incoming students with an iPad to providing each student with a MacBook Neo to better support the full range of academic work required at the University,” said Dr. Janie Diels, vice president for academic affairs. “Today’s students need technology that can seamlessly support everything from data analysis and research to presentations, writing, collaboration and creative projects. In particular, some courses and programs rely on the full desktop version of Microsoft Excel, including advanced features that are not available or are more limited on an iPad. By providing every student with a laptop capable of handling these demands, we’re ensuring they can fully engage in their coursework from the very beginning without worrying about whether they have the right technology. It’s an investment in student learning, confidence and long-term success.” Recently introduced by Apple, the MacBook Neo is a reliable, easy-to-use laptop designed for the demands of higher education. Featuring a 13-inch display and powered by Apple’s A18 Pro chip, the device provides the performance students need for research, coursework, multimedia projects and collaboration throughout their college careers. The initiative also supports a more seamless classroom experience by allowing faculty to design assignments and learning activities knowing every incoming student has access to the same technology and software capabilities. Students will be better equipped to participate in collaborative projects, complete assignments efficiently and take advantage of the University’s growing array of digital learning resources both inside and outside the classroom, according to University officials. Topics: Academic Support Share this story News Categories News Categories Select News Category About  (866) Academic Support  (34) Academics  (292) Accounting  (9) Admission  (32) Alumni  (219) Alumni Stories  (42) American Studies  (4) Art  (168) Athletics  (2,827) Bio