      "description": "Garcia '23 to Receive Young Alumni Service Award - University of the Ozarks Skip to main content Enable accessibility for low vision Open the accessibility menu Skip to main content Join us for Homecoming! October 15-18 Click here to check out the details! Ozarks Experience Ozarks Email Calendar Directory TSC Search Ozarks.edu: Narrow your search by content type Page Degrees Events News Offices & Services Faculty & Staff Links Menu University of the Ozarks Home Admissions & Aid Show sub-menu Learn about our admissions process, financial aid and begin your Ozarks journey. Admissions & Aid Costs & Aid How to Apply Visit Campus New Student Orientation & Move-In High School Juniors Incoming Freshman Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Calendar Apply Academics Show sub-menu Learn about our unique academic experience and the academic opportunities here at University of the Ozarks. Academics Our Academic Experience Degrees & Programs LENS Program Compass Study Abroad Library Canvas Student Success Center Jones Learning Center Faculty Directory Calendar Apply Life at Ozarks Show sub-menu Explore what makes life at Ozarks so special. Life at Ozarks Important Dates New Student Orientation & Move-In Student Engagement Residential Life & Housing Dining Shuttle Services Campus Recreation Spiritual Life Career Services Counseling Services Campus & Region Map Public Safety Title IX Calendar Apply Athletics Show sub-menu Our student-athletes strive for excellence on and off of the playing field, court or pool. Athletics Athletics Website Intercollegiate Sports Schedules Athlete Recruitment Eagle Tuesdays Fitness Facilities Support Athletics Recruit Me Support Show sub-menu Your gifts to University of the Ozarks truly matter to our students! Support Ways to Support Green Giving Update your info Grants and Initiatives Advancement Staff Hire an Eagle 1834 Society Planned Giving Give Bookstore Show sub-menu Our campus store located in Robson Library next to Campus Perks. Shop Now Conference Services Show sub-menu Ozarks offers a prime location for a variety of events. Contact us today to see how we can help make your next event a success. Conference Services Conferences and Meetings Weddings and Receptions Camps Catering Internal Events Contact Us! About Show sub-menu Learn about our thriving university, staff and history. About Leadership History Mission and Vision Our Christian Heritage Board of Trustees Rankings and Accreditations Student Outcomes Strategic Plan News Location & Directions Personnel Directory Offices & Services Marketing and Public Relations Reporting Calendar Request Info Search Ozarks.edu: Links Current Students Admitted Students Parents Faculty and Staff Alumni Search Request Info Visit Give Apply Home / News / Garcia ’23 to Receive Young Alumni Service Award Garcia ’23 to Receive Young Alumni Service Award 21 hours ago • September 14, 2026 By Larry Isch Posted in Alumni University of the Ozarks alumna Odalis Garcia ’23 of Springdale, Ark., will be honored by her alma mater with the 2026 Young Alumni Service Award during Homecoming Weekend, scheduled for October 16-18. The Young Alumni Service Award recognizes an alumnus who is at least five years out of graduation and under 35 years of age, has been active in alumni activities, and who has demonstrated loyalty to the University. The award will be presented at the Alumni Awards Banquet as part of Homecoming Weekend on Friday, October 16, 2026, in the Rogers Conference Center on the U of O campus. A native of Clarksville, Garcia graduated from Ozarks in 2023 with a degree in business administration. She currently serves as a realtor with PAK Home Realty in Northwest Arkansas. She also works in marketing and has owned and operated a photography business for the past six years. Garcia serves on the University of the Ozarks Alumni Board of Directors as well as on the board for the Hispanic Women’s Organization of Arkansas. She was recognized earlier this year as Volunteer of the Year by CASA of the 5th Judicial District for her service as a Court Appointed Special Advocate (CASA). Through her professional and volunteer work, she remains actively involved in supporting and strengthening her community. For more information about Homecoming Weekend 2026, please visit https://ozarks.edu/alumni/homecoming/ Topics: Alumni Share this story News Categories News Categories Select News Category About  (866) Academic Support  (34) Academics  (292) Accounting  (9) Admission  (32) Alumni  (219) Alumni Stories  (42) American Studies  (4) Art  (168) Athletics  (2,827) Biology  (73) Business Administration  (92) Business Education  (1) Campaign  (17) Campus Life  (39) Career Services  (17) Chapel  (46) Chemistry  (26) Communication Studies  (84) Community Events  (404) Community Service  (66) Computer Science  (6) Cost & Aid  (3) COVID-19  (8) Creative Writing / Thought  (6) Criminal Justice  (4) Donor Spotlights  (8) Economics  (3) Education  (73) Elementary Education  (12) English  (22) Environmental Studies  (39) Exercise Science  (1) Exhibit  (70) Faculty Spotlights  (51) Film Studies  (4) Finance  (1) Financial Aid  (15) Giving  (99) Graphic Design  (1) Greystone  (3) Health Science  (35) History  (13) Information Science  (2) Interfaith Studies  (14) International  (16) Internships  (21) JLC  (54) Management  (9) Marketing  (15) Mathematics  (35) Media Production  (8) Military Science  (3) Music  (52) Music Performance  (15) Music Studies  (4) Outdoors  (25) Parents  (9) PE  (4) Philosophy  (15) Photography  (5) Physical Education  (4) Physics  (7) Political Science  (48) Presbyterian  (47) Psychology  (40) Religion  (17) Robson Library  (2) ROTC  (2) Scholarship  (32) Skills Academy  (1) Sociology  (14) Spanish  (16) Strategic Communication  (3) Student Events  (126) Student Life  (35) Student Organizations  (100) Student Stories  (66) Student Support Services  (4) Study Abroad  (21) Sustainable Agricult